{{Deity|name=Anubis|title=The Hound of the Dead|symbol=Black jackal|alignment=Lawful Good|power=Unknown|pantheon=[[Pharaonic pantheon]]|home=[[Astral Plane]]|gender=Masculine|portfolio=Dead gods|cleric alignments=Any}}

'''Anubis''' was a wandering [[Pharaonic pantheon|Pharaonic]] power of unknown status. He was the guardian of the dead until [[Osiris]] was deified and took over Anubis's portfolio. In danger of being forgotten, he took to wandering the [[Astral Plane]] and guarding the still-potent corpses of dead powers. Anubis had no realm, just a throne to sit on and a book to take notes in. He was described as not quite a true deity, but rather something entirely unique among the cosmos.<ref>{{Cite book/On Hallowed Ground|87}}</ref>

